Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["  Phantom XXZ bulk: reduced edge state and Choi dynamics ", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"d6e27862-e894-9140-9ba1-2ca04d677c9a"],

Cell["\<\
  One self-contained .m workflow derived from the two supplied independent \
files. N denotes BULK spins; L=N+2 includes the two additional probes, A=1 \
and B=L. S=PauliMatrix/2, hbar=1, bit 0=up; natural-log entropies. The fixed \
transverse fields act ONLY on physical sites 2 and L-1. They remain present \
during evolution and do not depend on g or on either probe's state. The bulk \
helix is an eigenstate of the isolated, FIELD-DRESSED bulk; it need not be an \
eigenstate after attaching the probes at nonzero g. Evaluate the context cell \
first, shared definitions next, then verification. Chapters 1 (ZZ) and 2 \
(Exchange) have independent editable run settings. Both compute reduced-state \
dynamics and an input-independent Choi channel. There are no static scans or \
QST calculations. Get evaluates enabled runs. Disable MakePlots/ExportResults \
to compute without MaTeX or the front end. The uploaded vectors for \
N=4,...,10 are embedded; no .txt files are needed. IMPORTANT: transverse \
fields break bulk and total Sz conservation. Initial magnetization weights \
are reported, but magnetization slices are NOT evolved independently. Only \
exact invariant components with zero input overlap are skipped. ZZ still has \
four exact fixed-edge blocks; Exchange uses complex Hermitian ED on each \
reachable component, normally the full 2^(N+2) space. Energy conventions: \
this file keeps the benchmark H=J(XX+YY+Delta ZZ), with dimensionless \
Delta=Cos[gamma]. The screenshot uses dimensional Delta_z= J Cos[gamma]. Its \
bond energy is Delta_z/4. The .txt energies at J=1 equal -4 times this \
table's energy; both are displayed explicitly, never conflated. psiSpinCurMax \
is an approximate maximum-current preparation for positive J, not an exact \
optimizer; its current sign depends on J. It is retained as a separate \
supplied eigenvector: it is generally not the product helix, even though it \
lies at the same degenerate energy.  \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"154959c1-e15a-ba44-9def-a6c831181d33"],

